# Root .dockerignore — the Docker build context is the repo root (see
# .github/workflows/release.yml), so both backend/ and frontend/ images build
# from here and share this single ignore file. The per-package
# backend/.dockerignore and frontend/.dockerignore no longer take effect once
# the context is the root; everything relevant is consolidated here.

# Dependencies and build output (rebuilt inside the image) — matched at every
# depth so backend/, frontend/ and shared-contracts/ are all covered.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# Tests never belong in an image build.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.pbt.test.ts

# Local env and secrets — never ship these.
**/.env
**/.env.local

# Runtime/user data (backend vault storage etc.).
backend/data

# VCS, logs, editor/tooling metadata.
.git
.github
.kiro
**/npm-debug.log*

# NOTE: deliberately NOT ignoring *.md — backend/assets/ ships the welcome-vault
# templates, which ARE Markdown, and the backend image COPYs that directory.
